# Phase 07.8 — Attendee-Trusted TLS via nip.io + Let's Encrypt
#
# .acme-state holds the per-deploy LE cert wiring (DEPLOY_ID, STABLE_ACM_ARN,
# ALB_IP, NIP_FQDN_WRP, NIP_FQDN_BANKING) — written by Plan 04
# configure-workshop.sh ACME step, read by verify-tls.sh. Per D-10 this is
# local-only / never cached across cluster destroy → re-deploy cycles, and
# per the secrets-hygiene baseline it MUST be gitignored.
#
# Two entries:
#   - .acme-state                    : practical git-ignore semantic (file
#                                     resolved relative to this gitignore
#                                     i.e. infrastructure/.acme-state)
#   - infrastructure/.acme-state     : matches the verify-tls.sh harness
#                                     grep contract verbatim (Plan 01 Task 1
#                                     verification gate)
.acme-state
infrastructure/.acme-state

# Also ignore the idempotent-rerun marker (sibling file written by Plan 04
# configure-workshop.sh on the second run for verify-tls.sh --check
# idempotent-rerun / skip-acme-honored).
.acme-rerun-marker
infrastructure/.acme-rerun-marker
